==German==

===Etymology===
From {{affix|de|Erde|t1=earth, ground|Männchen|t2=little man}}, originally referring only to the gnome. The use for “meerkat” seems quite recent (perhaps not before the 1960s), though in German dialects it was already sometimes used metaphorically for animals, e.g. the mole.

